\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $W(r,k)$ be the least $N$ such that every coloring of $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ with $r$ colors contains a monochromatic arithmetic progression of length $k$. Determine the unknown exact values of $W(r,k)$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_unsolved_problems_in_mathematics#Combinatorics}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let $W(r,k)$ be the least $N$ such that every coloring of $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ with $r$ colors contains a monochromatic arithmetic progression of length $k$. Determine the unknown exact values of $W(r,k)$.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 3200015 (AMR-031-0015). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_unsolved_problems_in_mathematics#Combinatorics}.
\end{itemize}
